# Per-sample admixture

**What this is.** Two panels covering the cohort's admixture story.

- **Panel A** boxes the *dominant* and *other* proportions per
  FLARE top-1 ancestry stratum. Five strata × two boxes for SP5.
  Boxes span p5–p95 with the median bar in the middle; the dashed
  red reference at {{ "%.2f"|format(data.threshold_dominant if data.get("present") else 0.95) }} is the dominant
  threshold used in the cohort-structure section.
- **Panel B** is the classic ADMIXTURE-style per-sample stack,
  restricted to the *admixed* sub-cohort (top-1 < {{ "%.2f"|format(data.threshold_dominant if data.get("present") else 0.95) }}),
  sorted by top-1 ancestry then descending dominant proportion. The
  full-cohort version is omitted because at production cohort sizes
  it compresses to a coloured smear; the admixed subset is where the
  per-sample view actually carries information.

**How to read this chart.** Panel A: low *other* boxes mean the
stratum is genuinely homogeneous on chr1; an *other* box that pushes
into the 0.10+ range means a sizable fraction of the stratum is
non-trivially admixed. Panel B: long single-colour runs are mildly
admixed leaning samples; visible secondary colour bands are the
real two-/three-way mixes.

